.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt MT76 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mt76 ,
.Nm mt7921 ,
.Nm mt7925
.Nd MediaTek IEEE 802.11 wireless network drivers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
The drivers will auto-load without any user interaction using
.Xr devmatch 8
if enabled in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.Pp
Only if auto-loading is explicitly disabled, place the following
line in
.Xr rc.conf 5
to manually load a driver as a module at boot time:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kld_list="${kld_list} if_mt7925"
.Ed
.Pp
The drivers should not be compiled into the kernel.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
family of drivers provides support for MediaTek PCIe wireless network
devices.
The drivers are ports of the Linux mt76 drivers and use the
.Xr linuxkpi 4
compatibility layer and
.Xr net80211 4 .
.Pp
.Nm mt76_core
contains the code shared by all chipsets and is loaded automatically
as a dependency.
The chipset specific modules are:
.Bl -tag -width "if_mt7925" -offset indent
.It Nm if_mt7921
MT7921 and MT7922 (Wi-Fi 6/6E) devices.
.It Nm if_mt7925
MT7925 (Wi-Fi 7) devices.
.El
.Pp
Modules for mt7615, mt7915 and mt7996 are built as well but have not
been tested on
.Mx .
.Pp
The compatibility layer currently supports 802.11 a/b/g/n/ac;
802.11ax, 802.11be, 6GHz and multi-link operation are not supported,
so a Wi-Fi 6 or Wi-Fi 7 device associates using 802.11ac at most.
Only station mode is supported.
.Pp
For more information on configuring this device, see
.Xr ifconfig 8
and
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8 .
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm if_mt7925
driver has been tested with the MediaTek MT7925 (PCI ID 14c3:7925).
.Sh FILES
The firmware is part of the base system and is loaded automatically as
kernel modules named after the firmware file, for example
.Pa /boot/kernel/WIFI_RAM_CODE_MT7925_1_1.bin.ko .
Firmware files placed in
.Pa /boot/firmware/mediatek/
are used instead if present.
.Pp
The firmware comes from the linux-firmware repository and is
distributed under the MediaTek firmware license
.Pq Pa sys/contrib/dev/mt76fw/LICENCE.mediatek ,
which allows redistribution for use with devices containing MediaTek
chipsets.
.Sh LOADER TUNABLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va compat.linuxkpi.80211.hw_crypto
Use the hardware for 802.11 encryption and decryption.
The default is
.Sy 1 .
Setting it to
.Sy 0
switches to software crypto, which also disables receive A-MPDU
aggregation and roughly halves throughput.
.It Va compat.linuxkpi.skb.mem_limit
Limit network buffer memory to physical addresses below 4GB
.Pq Sy 1
or 64GB
.Pq Sy 2 .
These devices use 32-bit DMA, so on machines with more than 4GB of
memory this is set to
.Sy 1
automatically when the driver attaches.
An explicit setting in
.Xr loader.conf 5
takes precedence.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "failed to get patch semaphore"
The device does not answer firmware commands; usually the firmware
could not be loaded or the device is in a bad state.
Reboot and check that the firmware files are installed.
.It "Failed to send patch"
The firmware download to the device failed.
On machines with more than 4GB of memory check that
.Va compat.linuxkpi.skb.mem_limit
has not been set to
.Sy 0
and that
.Va compat.linuxkpi.lkpi_pci_nseg1_fail
does not increase.
.It "hardware init failed"
Firmware initialisation failed after several retries.
The driver stays loaded without a network interface.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr iwlwifi 4 ,
.Xr linuxkpi 4 ,
.Xr rtw88 4 ,
.Xr wlan 4 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
drivers first appeared in
.Mx 4.2 .
.Sh BUGS
Throughput is lower than on other operating systems.
